WEBVTT

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:09.400
Target altitude reached.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.830
<i>Okay. We're switching to scenario 2-A.</i>

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:14.680
<i>Gripen, switch to flight mode "jagt."</i>

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:18.410
<i>You will encounter the enemy in 30 seconds.</i>

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:19.690
<i>EPCM is active.</i>

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.090
Roger.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:25.440
Switching to autonomous 
mode due to EPCM effects.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.020
<i>Begin the mission!</i>

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.430
Merge!

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:12.110
<i>Komatsu Air Force Base</i>

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:17.820
<i>Anima Core</i>

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:16.650
We're only at the simulator stage,
and look at her.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:21.280
B-But this is after she's been awake 
longer than usual for her.

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:23.280
Her consciousness level was stable.

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:28.740
Yeah. Thanks to you,
our Sleeping Beauty has improved a lot.

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:33.850
But "being awake" and "being able to pilot 
a plane" are two very different things.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:35.840
We're nowhere near where we need to be.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:38.080
Upsetting.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:42.230
I don't want you thinking that 
this is my true strength.

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:43.580
Damn right.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:46.320
If you perform like that 
at the test next week,

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:49.400
I'll sign the paperwork to scrap 
you right then and there.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:52.940
But this isn't anything like a Daughter.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:55.270
I can't fly right in this thing.

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:58.040
Wow, this setup is incredible.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:02:59.400
What don't you like?

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.920
The control systems are all wrong.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.290
It's slow to respond.

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:05.720
There's no feedback from external stimuli.

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:10.250
We rushed to get that thing made.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:14.230
And that NFI only got 
added after it was built.

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:15.620
NFI?

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:18.180
That.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:21.380
Those things on both sides 
of the seat are the NFI.

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:23.430
The Neural Fusion Interface.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:27.560
It links the Daughter's controls 
with your sensory organs.

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:31.320
It expands your neural network out 
to the very tip of the airframe.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.380
So you can fly with just a thought?

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.060
Not quite.

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:38.440
It's the same way a human moves their limbs.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:42.030
If you want to move to the right, 
the elevons will activate.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:45.210
If you want to decelerate, 
the engines will decrease their output.

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:48.140
Wow, that's amazing.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:52.530
Wait, does that mean that if you 
had to pilot a plane like normal,

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:54.390
you'd be really bad at it?

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:57.050
Your lack of understanding shocks me.

00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:00.420
Your ignorance exceeds my imagination 
and inspires me to rage.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:02.360
You should try it too, then.

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:03.870
No, I...

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.420
Go ahead.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:09.480
We need to reset all the settings, anyway.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.980
You've flown a Cessna, right?

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:16.520
The die has been cast.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:24.200
Wow... this skips almost all 
of the pre-flight checklist!

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:28.340
The airframe computer will auto-adjust 
its own attitude to a certain degree.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:30.080
Pretty handy, right?

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.400
Well, even if you crash, you'll live.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.280
So don't worry about a thing.

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:47.550
<i>You've got good instincts.</i>

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:49.550
<i>I thought you'd have a harder time with it.</i>

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:53.900
If this was a real plane, 
I'd be too scared to do anything.

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:56.300
Pretty impressive, though.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:58.600
Oh no...

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:06.520
<i>Flying in an empty sky 
is pretty dull, right?</i>

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:09.450
Seriously?

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:11.380
<i>If that thing gets on your six,
you're a dead man.</i>

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:12.410
That's not fair!

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:26.710
Fine! I'll let it get ahead of me 
and shoot it down from behind!

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:41.660
I managed to get it in front of me,

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:44.260
but it's hard to get the plane 
back into the fight quickly.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:45.850
Kei.

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:47.970
I demand an explanation.

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:51.830
Everyone says that your flying 
is more stable than mine.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:55.070
Impossible. You must have 
been cheating somehow!

00:05:55.070 --> 00:05:56.430
No way.

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:58.730
Anyway, this thing is really easy to fly.

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:00.680
It's not defective at all.

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:05.890
It feels like I could pilot the real thing 
if I had a few more tries with this.

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:09.220
Well?

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.420
That was an amazing experience.

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:15.100
Can I try it again sometime?

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:18.220
Sure, depending on how Gripen's looking.

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:21.280
Her test flight is in seven days, after all.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.070
Oh, I see.

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:26.190
Okay, let's both do our best!

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:30.510
Why are you telling me what to do?

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:42.330
<b>Sunoken</b>

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:28.380
<b>No Smoking</b>

00:07:31.070 --> 00:07:33.640
We figured out why Gripen's 
been doing better.

00:07:34.570 --> 00:07:38.380
Or more precisely, we figured 
out what's going on.

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:39.600
But...

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:42.090
Look at this.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:46.680
This is Gripen's EGG graph.

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:49.210
Her brainwave pattern, essentially.

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:53.350
It's started to get unstable.

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:53.810
Yes.

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:58.570
When this unstable state continues, 
she loses consciousness.

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:00.410
But...

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:03.990
The graph below shows your brain waves.

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:07.840
When Gripen's EGG graph is 
influenced by your brain waves...

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:10.220
This is...

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:13.460
The oscillation synchronizes, 
and it stabilizes.

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:17.480
It happens whenever you're 
within about ten meters.

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:21.860
We'll need to get some more 
data to find the exact number.

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:27.730
But it's impossible for someone's 
brain waves to synchronize

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:30.200
with someone else's without 
even a millisecond of lag.

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:34.850
Not unless the patterns were 
established in advance.

00:08:35.350 --> 00:08:37.740
Established in advance?

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:42.290
Let me ask you something.

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:46.570
You never met her before 
you left Shanghai, right?

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:48.420
No...

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:52.230
Well, whatever.

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:56.640
As long as you're near her, she's stable.

00:08:57.130 --> 00:08:59.800
All we need to do now is adjust 
the intervals where she's awake.

00:09:00.590 --> 00:09:05.920
We can't have you going up in the air with 
her to keep her stable, after all.

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:13.750
Hey. Sounds like you're doing good.

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:15.160
Thanks to you.

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:17.790
When you are near, I feel better.

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:27.250
<b>Cafeteria</b>

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:27.250
<b>Sea of Japan</b>

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:20.750
I'm not doing anything, though.

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:24.260
But if you're doing this well, I bet 
not only could you pass the test,

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:27.250
you could do a real fight!

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:30.210
<b>Today's Menu</b>

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:30.210
I will do my best to live 
up to your expectations.

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:35.740
When the Xi are gone, I hope 
we can fly in China together.

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:37.250
China?

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:42.840
I used to live in a town in China called 
Changshu 'cause of my dad's job.

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:44.270
Changshu...

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:46.670
It's northwest of Shanghai.

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:49.190
There's lots of factories and labs.

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:51.360
<b>Hand-To-Mouth Travel Diary</b>

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:51.480
<b>These are pictures of Changshu, China,
 where I went last month. The food was great, too!</b>

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:53.100
There's a lot of old buildings left, 
and it's a really laid-back place.

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:55.420
Maybe it's similar to Komatsu.

00:09:56.880 --> 00:09:58.070
Ten days ago?

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.740
<b>Topics</b>

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.740
<b>Society</b>

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.740
<b>Politics</b>

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.740
<b>International</b>

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.740
<b>Sports</b>

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.740
<b>Column</b>

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.950
<b>International</b>

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:00.280
<b>On the 8th of this month, Changshu, a city in Jiangsu, China, was destroyed in a
 Xi attack. A photograph of the city of Changshu, China on June 8th.
 The scale of the destruction can be seen.</b>

00:10:02.020 --> 00:10:03.910
<i>Those bastards.</i>

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:07.680
<i>They destroyed the whole city!</i>

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:10.160
<i>This is awful.</i>

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:13.370
<i>Why did they have to go this far?</i>

00:10:14.020 --> 00:10:17.210
<i>They didn't need to destroy every 
building in the city, did they?</i>

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:21.680
<i>The city of Changshu was wiped 
from the face of the earth.</i>

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:23.680
Kei?

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:25.040
Kei?

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:27.570
Oh, sorry.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:29.190
Are you sick?

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:30.810
No, I'm fine.

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:33.680
I have a present for you.

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:35.220
What is this?

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:37.040
It would be embarrassing 
if you opened it here.

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:38.330
Open it at home.

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:41.260
You always do so much for me.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:42.330
So it's my way of saying thanks.

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:44.660
Okay, I'll take it.

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:46.170
Thanks.

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:48.400
Okay.

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:50.600
Let's go, then.

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:51.360
Okay.

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:53.580
Thank you for the meal.

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:54.900
You're welcome!

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:56.480
Thank you for the meal.

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:57.500
Sure thing!

00:10:58.060 --> 00:10:59.460
I'm sorry—

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:02.340
Why aren't you locked up somewhere?

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:05.150
How come they let you walk freely?

00:11:05.150 --> 00:11:05.920
I...

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:06.850
Don't talk!

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:09.380
Stop looking at me with that
 face! You're not one of us!

00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:10.920
What are you doing?

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:13.160
Who are you?

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:16.440
I'm helping with the work
they're doing on her.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:20.490
Oh, so you're just like the TRDI, then.

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:23.690
Don't even let us see that thing!

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:25.080
That's right!

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.000
Stop it. You're acting like a little kid.

00:11:28.610 --> 00:11:33.740
She's being sent on dangerous missions 
when she's not feeling well!

00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:36.970
Don't say anything else to piss us off!

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:40.330
There's no reason for you to be so mean.

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:42.100
Kei, let's go.

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:45.030
Wait, do you not know?

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:46.730
Know what?

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:49.130
Know what she's made of.

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:50.390
Kei!

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:54.300
Anima are made of parts salvaged from Xi
 after they've been shot down.

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:00.900
Gripen...

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:03.060
Well, if you didn't know—

00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:04.040
Gripen!

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:11.060
<i>The rain didn't stop for 
the next three days.</i>

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:17.710
<i>2 years ago, Karamay Airport</i>

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:35.440
Stop it! Stop, please!

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:40.300
Mom!

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:44.240
Mom!

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:05.480
What the hell was that?

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:16.080
<i>Her test flight's today, huh?</i>

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:16.480
<b>6/21 (Wed)</b>

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:25.400
<i>Yashirodoori said they're 
still researching the Anima.</i>

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:27.900
<i>In other words, they're a black box.</i>

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:32.470
<i>They recovered some kind of Xi computer 
or something from their planes,</i>

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:35.430
<i>and put it in manmade airplanes.</i>

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:39.030
<i>Even though they don't know when 
they'll go back to being monsters...</i>

00:13:39.990 --> 00:13:42.960
Why aren't you locked up somewhere?

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:45.560
How come they let you walk free—

00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:49.250
Anima are made of parts salvaged from Xi
 after they've been shot down.

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:53.020
<i>Now I understand what that officer meant.</i>

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:57.430
<i>But what are they going to do?</i>

00:13:57.950 --> 00:14:00.190
<i>Are they going to fly as planned?</i>

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:02.830
<i>No point in thinking about it.</i>

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:05.010
<i>There's only an hour until her test flight.</i>

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:09.150
<i>Even if I went, they'd just ask 
what the hell I was doing there.</i>

00:14:09.150 --> 00:14:17.370
<b>What Do They Want!?
Mysterious Military Group
The Xi!!</b>

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:17.370
<b>Breaking News: Seventh Fleet Vanishes</b>

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:11.890
<i>Breaking news.</i>

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:17.380
<i>The Seventh Fleet, which was sent to deal 
with the Chinese civil war, has vanished.</i>

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:20.340
<i>The safety of Japanese citizens 
in China, as well as the refugees</i>

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:24.210
<i>who were scheduled to evacuate 
is unknown, and attempts...</i>

00:14:21.850 --> 00:14:22.990
Morning.

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:26.970
"Morning"? It's almost noon!

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:30.010
No work today?

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:31.430
Nope.

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:35.710
Then want to go shopping?

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:37.780
Maybe get your mind off things?

00:14:37.780 --> 00:14:39.880
Sure. Let's go.

00:14:39.880 --> 00:14:40.660
Really?

00:14:40.660 --> 00:14:41.780
Yeah.

00:14:41.780 --> 00:14:43.150
Want to leave now?

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:44.650
I can go get changed.

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:46.380
Okay!

00:14:53.140 --> 00:14:56.540
<i>Why do I have to feel guilty?</i>

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:58.900
<i>She lied to me.</i>

00:15:00.610 --> 00:15:03.370
<i>A muffler? It's June.</i>

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:12.760
H-Hey! Kei?

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:13.810
Are we going shopping?

00:15:13.810 --> 00:15:15.040
Next time!

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:18.220
Kei, you jerk!

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:24.650
<i>Kei, thank you for everything.</i>

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:30.780
<i>Because of you, I'm not 
scared of flying anymore.</i>

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:33.230
<i>I'll do my best on my test flight.</i>

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:37.540
<i>I told someone at the TRDI 
that I wanted to thank you,</i>

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:42.470
<i>and they said, "Give him something 
handmade! Guys always fall for that,"</i>

00:15:42.470 --> 00:15:45.980
<i>so I read a lot of books, and then 
decided to make a muffler for you.</i>

00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:47.860
<i>Did you fall for it?</i>

00:15:48.620 --> 00:15:52.210
<i>I need to apologize to you.</i>

00:15:52.210 --> 00:15:56.000
<i>I've been hiding something big from you.</i>

00:15:56.770 --> 00:16:00.310
<i>I'm made from Xi parts.</i>

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:05.300
<i>I'm told they extracted the core from 
a crashed Xi and grew me in a tube,</i>

00:16:05.300 --> 00:16:07.600
<i>using it as part of my spine.</i>

00:16:08.140 --> 00:16:12.640
<i>I can't really explain what 
makes me different than a Xi.</i>

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:18.690
<i>But... I want you to know that 
I have no memories of being a Xi.</i>

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:22.410
<i>My first memories are of being Gripen,</i>

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:24.660
<i>and telling myself I had 
to protect humanity.</i>

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:31.070
<i>I fly for humanity,
and I fight for humanity.</i>

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:33.480
<i>I thought that was normal.</i>

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:38.700
<i>Because that's why the JAS39 was created.</i>

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:44.100
<i>I was going to tell you this sooner...</i>

00:16:44.680 --> 00:16:47.220
<i>But when we went to the shrine,</i>

00:16:47.220 --> 00:16:49.780
<i>you said you hated the Xi,</i>

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:51.520
<i>so I didn't.</i>

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:54.350
<i>I didn't want you to hate me.</i>

00:16:56.480 --> 00:16:59.440
<i>But I can't keep lying forever.</i>

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:03.300
<i>So I used all my courage 
to write this letter.</i>

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:07.880
<i>I'm praying you'll come 
to see me tomorrow.</i>

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:11.250
<i>I hate the Xi.</i>

00:17:15.480 --> 00:17:18.960
But I don't hate you!

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:24.930
<i>Komatsu Tower, Barbie 01 
is ready for departure.</i>

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:28.390
I'm sorry... I...

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:32.860
Did you read her letter?

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:35.090
Yes, this morning.

00:17:35.810 --> 00:17:39.700
And you decided to show up 'cause of it, huh?

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:41.580
You really are easy.

00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:48.350
But... that's how she really feels.

00:17:48.350 --> 00:17:52.750
Those are her words, not the 
words of a program or a Xi.

00:17:53.140 --> 00:17:56.110
That, at least, I want you to understand.

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:57.480
Right...

00:17:58.250 --> 00:18:00.250
Can she fly?

00:18:00.250 --> 00:18:02.090
It's a bit of a brute-force method,

00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:05.740
but we put her to sleep so she'd 
be awake when we needed her.

00:18:06.930 --> 00:18:09.970
We can probably at least fool them 
for the duration of the test flight.

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:12.730
<i>Barbie 01, this is Komatsu Tower.</i>

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:15.170
You are cleared for takeoff on Runway 06.

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:15.950
<i>Roger.</i>

00:18:16.250 --> 00:18:20.990
<i>Barbie 01, cleared for takeoff on Runway 06.</i>

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:22.400
Why do you act like she's 
so important to you?

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:25.880
I don't like it when I don't 
understand something.

00:18:26.760 --> 00:18:29.980
Why is she the only one that has problems?

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:33.590
Why does being with you fix them?

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:37.270
Moving on to the next option

00:18:37.270 --> 00:18:41.880
without trying to figure out why 
this one failed is what monkeys do.

00:18:42.270 --> 00:18:44.340
And we ain't monkeys.

00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:51.900
<i>Barbie 01 has entered the mission area.</i>

00:18:53.280 --> 00:18:55.010
First, let's try out your guns.

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:58.440
You'll be in range of the first target soon.

00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:01.160
<i>Roger. I'll end this in a single strike.</i>

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:03.300
It's bugging her.

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:06.190
I told her to stay calm.

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:09.810
Barbie 01 is approaching Target 01.

00:19:09.810 --> 00:19:11.400
Three miles to contact.

00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:12.470
Two.

00:19:13.700 --> 00:19:14.710
One.

00:19:16.520 --> 00:19:17.840
<i>Target kill.</i>

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:18.830
Kill copy.

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:20.350
She did it!

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:23.730
Okay, now try your AAMs.

00:19:23.730 --> 00:19:28.530
Target 02, 020, 45, alt 25.

00:19:28.820 --> 00:19:29.790
<i>Roger.</i>

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:32.800
<i>Target 02. Mark 015.</i>

00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:35.110
<i>42.  Alt 28.</i>

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:37.340
Xi on radar!

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:39.320
Air superiority type. One unit!

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:40.530
Impossible!

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:42.490
We're nowhere near the East China Sea!

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:45.340
Bogey will reach our airspace in ten minutes.

00:19:45.340 --> 00:19:46.450
<i>I'll go!</i>

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:47.680
No!

00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:50.770
That plane's got nothing but 
training weapons on it.

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:52.590
Call Phantom from Misawa!

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:54.630
<i>They won't make it in time.</i>

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:57.330
<i>Target 02 priority registration deleted.</i>

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:01.290
Barbie 01 has veered off course!

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:05.610
It's been 45 minutes since she activated.

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:08.760
Irregularities on the direct link!

00:20:10.900 --> 00:20:13.740
<i>Static is amplifying... 
Error counter rising!</i>

00:20:15.970 --> 00:20:17.240
Gripen!

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:19.780
EGG pattern is showing instability!

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:21.650
Send a forced awakening signal!

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:24.450
<i>Charge 100! Shoot!</i>

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:28.070
It's no good. She's not responding!

00:20:30.030 --> 00:20:31.620
Activate the autopilot!

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:33.930
Get her the hell out of the combat area!

00:20:33.930 --> 00:20:35.370
Where is Phantom?

00:20:35.850 --> 00:20:39.100
Anima and Daughter are 
both under maintenance.

00:20:39.100 --> 00:20:41.930
It'll be one hour, minimum, 
before it can take off.

00:20:42.310 --> 00:20:45.050
Then tell the US military 
it's an emergency.

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:47.350
Radar warning!

00:20:47.670 --> 00:20:50.350
Bogey is on Barbie 01's tail!

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:54.780
<i>Gripen, wake up!</i>

00:20:55.240 --> 00:20:56.420
<i>Gripen!</i>

00:20:57.840 --> 00:20:59.180
They've locked on!

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:01.140
Gripen, wake up!

00:21:04.110 --> 00:21:06.100
Gripen!

00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:11.900
Looks like I'll have to help you, then.

00:21:24.130 --> 00:21:25.500
Gotcha!

00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:28.380
Fox 2, go!

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:32.360
Splash!

00:21:32.360 --> 00:21:34.280
Bogey is down.

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:36.930
What was that?

00:21:37.670 --> 00:21:39.940
She was waiting for the right 
moment to make her entrance.

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:41.360
Show-off.

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:44.060
<i>Daddy! Hi there!</i>

00:21:46.330 --> 00:21:49.980
<i>Looks like things were bad for 
a second, but it's okay now!</i>

00:21:50.890 --> 00:21:54.450
Eagle will protect the Sea of Japan!

00:23:27.450 --> 00:23:30.220
Next time on <i>Girly Air Force</i>...

00:23:30.220 --> 00:23:33.500
ALT 04: "The World You See."

00:23:30.550 --> 00:23:39.980
<i>The World You See</i>

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:37.980
Barbie 01 cleared for... take off!
